cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the Need-to-Know protocol, please cite it as below."
title: "Need-to-Know (NTK): an output-side protocol for what AI agents may say to other agents"
abstract: >-
  The Need-to-Know (NTK) protocol specifies what an AI agent may say to other agents.
  Each fact carries a label (public, role:<r>, private), each request carries
  requester, role and purpose, and each reply passes three checks: who is asking and why,
  use it but don't say it, and a hint check against inference. Replies are logged in a
  disclosure ledger and consent grants expire. NTK extends the Human Context Protocol (HCP)
  with output-side rules.
type: software
authors:
